# ludic.missions - jobs, contact missions, heists, races and adversary modes as data graphs: a mission
# is rows of nodes and edges, a run is an instance per lobby or team with objective state, markers as
# facts, checkpoints, roles and cuts, and player-made races and modes are the same rows. Uses
# ludic.base and nothing else. See README.md.
package "ludic.missions"
version "0.1.0"
kind source
